  "term": "biological clock",
  "definition": "The biological clock is a group of neurons in the suprachiasmatic nuclei of the hypothalamus that act as self-sustained oscillators. It generates rhythmic patterns of gene activity and electrical activity that help align the body’s circadian rhythms with the 24-hour day–night cycle.",
